            <title>[LU-21116] sanity test_900: lustre_rmmod: osc module in use, FAILed to clean up (review-ldiskfs-arm)</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21116</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;sanity test_900 (umount should not race with any mgc requeue thread) fails in review-ldiskfs-arm (rocky9.8 aarch64 client) with "test_900 returned 20". Its cleanup/setup ends with:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;lustre_rmmod: wait 40s for osc (refcnt 1)&lt;br/&gt;
rmmod: ERROR: Module osc is in use&lt;br/&gt;
FAILed to clean up&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The client is left with osc loaded and unmounted, so the following tests fail: sanity test_901 (umount failed), test_905 and test_912 (setstripe failed), test_908b (changelog_mask=+hsm failed), and sanity-lnet ("Failed to unload modules before test execution") and sanity-sec (test_setup, mountmds failed) in the same session.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The client dmesg shows the MGC requeue thread sleeping in mgc_process_log() on fail_loc 0x903 (cfs_fail_timeout id 903, 20000ms) while the client is unmounted.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The same failure was seen on 2026-11-03 on three unrelated changes and builds, all review-ldiskfs-arm: 69937 ps6 (build 135223, rev 0d91b3d7378e), 70293 ps2 (build 135214, rev fda29565a127) and 69970 ps2 (build 135203, rev ee605b26eb61). Other changes in this configuration passed test_900 in 1287 of 1290 runs over 30 days. The three changes touch HSM counters, osc writeback CPT and lctl parameter reads, none of which relates to module refcounts.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Failing test sets: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/b3763421-138d-4b29-8da7-29f0c6f87cdd" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/b3763421-138d-4b29-8da7-29f0c6f87cdd&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-69970-ps3-c43ccc0ab8a0 on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/69970" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/69970&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
